---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc. and the Rex Autistikōn Labs website: what we collect, how collaborator data are handled, and how to request access or correction."
>
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-500 mb-10">Effective date: 31 August 2026</p>

      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        This policy describes how Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc. handles information
        when you use <a href="https://rexautistikonlabs.org" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">rexautistikonlabs.org</a>.
        It is written in plain language. It is not a clinic privacy notice, because this
        organization is not a clinic.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Who controls this site</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The data controller is:
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc.<br />
        1485 Fouraker Rd #2402<br />
        Jacksonville, FL 32221<br />
        United States<br />
        <a
          href="mailto:info@rexautistikonlabs.org"
          data-analytics-event="contact_email_click"
          class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800"
        >info@rexautistikonlabs.org</a>
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Rex Autistikōn Labs is the research initiative operated by the Foundation. This site
        is operated for the Foundation’s research, publication, collaboration, and nonprofit
        operations.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">What we collect</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-slate-600 space-y-3 mb-10">
        <li>
          <strong>Server logs and security records.</strong> Our host (Azure Static Web Apps
          and related Microsoft Azure services) may record IP address, date and time, requested
          path, referrer, and browser or device type. These records are used to operate, secure,
          and debug the site.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form fields.</strong> If you use the Foundation contact form, we
          receive name, institutional email, role, topic, and message. Submissions are delivered
          by email to info@rexautistikonlabs.org. A form-delivery processor may transmit that
          message on our behalf.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Collaborator access-request fields.</strong> If you request platform access,
          we receive investigator name, institutional email, organization, role, optional
          department, intended use, IRB/ethics status, preferred start date, and the compliance
          acknowledgements you check.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Microsoft sign-in for approved collaborators.</strong> The collaborator portal
          (including Data Intake, Results, and admin tools) requires Microsoft Entra ID sign-in.
          Microsoft authenticates the account. We receive the identity needed to authorize access
          for approved collaborators only. Submitting a request does not itself provision access.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Collaborator research data.</strong> Approved collaborators may submit coded
          measurement data through the secure intake tools. Those data are stored in a secure
          Azure environment controlled by the Foundation. They are not shared outside approved
          collaborators without written agreement.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Donation processor data.</strong> Gifts are processed on Zeffy’s domain, not
          on this site. Zeffy collects payment and donor information needed to complete the
          transaction. The Foundation does not store full card numbers. We may receive donor
          name, contact details, gift amount, and receipt information from Zeffy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional measurement tags.</strong> If Google Analytics 4 (and, if linked,
          Google Ads conversion tags) are configured for this site, those tools may collect
          page views and named events described in our internal tracking notes. This is optional
          measurement for nonprofit operations and advertising accountability. If a measurement
          ID is not configured, those tags are not loaded.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Essential cookies or similar storage may be used for security and for Microsoft sign-in
        on protected collaborator routes. If Google Analytics 4 or Google Ads conversion tags
        are enabled, Google may set cookies or use similar storage to count visits and
        advertising outcomes. We do not use those tags to measure time on page, scroll depth,
        or use of the interactive model. We do not run Google AdSense.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Microsoft Entra / collaborator portal</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Access to <a href="/intake" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">/intake</a>,
        <a href="/results" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">/results</a>, and
        administrative collaborator tools is restricted to authenticated, approved accounts.
        Sign-in is handled by Microsoft Entra ID. The Foundation assigns access after review.
        Portal use is for legitimate scientific research consistent with the Labs’ programme.
        See <a href="/how-to-collaborate" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">How to Collaborate</a>
        and <a href="/collaboration-governance" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">Collaboration Governance</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Collaborator research data</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Research data submitted by approved collaborators are stored in a secure Azure
        environment controlled by Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc. They are not sold.
        They are not shared outside approved collaborators without explicit written agreement.
        Direct identifiers of research participants are not required by the platform; collaborators
        remain responsible for their own ethics/IRB obligations. Further detail is on the
        <a href="/irb-faq" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">IRB &amp; Ethics FAQ</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Donations</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        The donate button on this site sends you to Zeffy on a third-party domain. Payment
        details are handled by Zeffy. The Foundation does not store full card numbers. Zeffy’s
        own privacy terms apply to that checkout. Return to this domain after a gift, if
        configured, does not by itself prove that a payment completed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">We do not sell personal data</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        The Foundation does not sell personal information. We do not share personal information
        for cross-context behavioral advertising. Optional measurement, when enabled, is used
        to understand whether public information and nonprofit advertising on this domain are
        reaching the intended audiences.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Retention</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Server logs are kept as needed for security and operations. Contact correspondence is
        kept as organizational records for as long as needed to respond and to maintain a record
        of the inquiry. Collaborator access records and research data are retained according to
        the written collaboration arrangements and applicable research record requirements.
        Donor records received from Zeffy are retained as needed for tax, accounting, and
        acknowledgment.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Access and correction</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        To request access to personal information we hold about you, or to ask for a correction,
        email
        <a
          href="mailto:info@rexautistikonlabs.org"
          data-analytics-event="contact_email_click"
          class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800"
        >info@rexautistikonlabs.org</a>.
        We may need to verify that the request comes from the right person.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Children</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        This site is not directed at children. Collaborator intake is institutional: we expect
        requests from researchers and other adults acting for universities, laboratories, or
        similar organizations. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
        through this website.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Where we are based</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        The Foundation is a United States organization. The site is hosted in Microsoft Azure
        regions used for our operations. Visitors from outside the United States may use the
        public pages. If you are such a visitor and have questions about international transfer
        or our handling of your information, contact info@rexautistikonlabs.org.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Changes</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        We may update this policy. The effective date above will change when we do. The current
        version will be posted at this URL.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6">
        Related:
        <a href="/transparency" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">Transparency &amp; Legal</a>
        ·
        <a href="/about" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">About the Foundation</a>
        ·
        <a href="/contact" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
